// Title: Hide Schedule Task Via Index Value Tamper
// Sigma ID: 5b16df71-8615-4f7f-ac9b-6c43c0509e61
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-26 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects when the "index" value of a scheduled task is modified from the registry Which
//   effectively hides it from any tooling such as "schtasks /query" (Read the referenced link for
//   more information about the effects of this technique)
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://blog.qualys.com/vulnerabilities-threat-research/2022/06/20/defending-against-scheduled-task-attacks-in-windows-environments
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_hide_scheduled_task_via_index_tamper.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Schedule\\TaskCache\\Tree.*$" and RegistryKey contains "Index") and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
